<title>UK: Lehman leads $930 million AT&amp;T asset-backed FRNs.</title>
<headline>Lehman leads $930 million AT&amp;T asset-backed FRNs.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following floating-rate issues were announced by lead manager Lehman Brothers International.</p>
<p> BORROWER   AT&amp;T UNIVERSAL CARD MASTERTRUST</p>
<p> AMT	  $850 MLN  BASE	 3M-LIBOR  MATURITY   *17.APR.02</p>
<p> TYPE	 FRN	 MARGIN     **	  PAY DATE    14.MAY.97</p>
<p> MOODY	AAA	 ISS PRICE  **	  FULL FEES   =</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AAA	 REOFFER    **</p>
<p> NOTES     *EXPECTED MATURITY. LEGAL MATURITY IS 19.APR.04.</p>
<p>	    **TO BEPRICED LATER AT 3ML +8-9 B.P.</p>
<p>+ + +</p>
<p> AMT	  $80 MLN   BASE	 3M-LIBOR  MATURITY   *17.APR.02</p>
<p> TYPE	 FRN	 MARGIN     **	  PAY DATE    14.MAY.97</p>
<p> MOODY	A2	  ISS PRICE  **	  FULL FEES   =</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  A	   REOFFER    **</p>
<p> NOTES     *EXPECTED MATURITY. LEGAL MATURITY IS 19.APR.04.</p>
<p>	    **TO BE PRICED LATER AT 3ML +28-29 B.P.</p>
<p>-- Dan Lalor, London newsroom +44 171 542 8863</p>
</text>
